{
  "_doc": "PLACEHOLDER — the reinterp SPACE STATES as ordered deltas over data/room/era1.json (the shipped EraMorph grammar). Session 12 (Sérgio Round 22, his wedge drawing): the space is a HEXAGON ALIGNED TO THE THREE 120° FACINGS, hub = the player's chair (0, ·, 0.7). Each 120° turn faces a perpendicular back wall — desk in front of you, the rest of that room around it. FURNITURE IS THE LIMITER between rooms (bookcase run, wardrobe-closet, dressers — no interior walls). r1 = reinterp E1 (witness furniture out; real door + record terminal on a repainted spine). r2 = THE CLUSTER opens at T1 (per the narrative master script): front wedge = the LEAD room (Daniel's, later Vera's — his furniture re-sorts forward as the space is re-partitioned); WEST wedge (yaw 120) = the parallel-tracks bay (sends s1/s3; Daniel's boxes land here at E3); EAST wedge (yaw 240) = the trans-facet room (sends s2/s4; the fluid niche stands on its back wall via fluid_niche.json). The rear face (180°) is the SPINE — door + terminal — kept clear as a sight channel between the two rear bays. r4 = E4: Maya's desk rises IN the channel beside the terminal (the person and the record share a wall), the LAMP moves to her desk, the window goes dark for good. Every side room's screen faces the HUB — the player reads each room over its occupant's shoulder. COLOR LAW: every hex exists in era1.json. yaw = y-rotation degrees (wedges are rectilinear in their own frame, rotated whole — the only non-90° angles in the piece, structural). Session 13 (Round 23): both side wedges are FULL ROOMS at the lead room's density (window+curtains+posters+headboard bed+4-leg desk+shelf); limiter furniture moved OUT of the seat sightlines — tall wardrobes flat against the shared 60/300 faces, only chest-height runs (h 0.55) near the middle, and the rooms' own beds bound the rear. Generator recipe: scratchpad gen_radial2.mjs; nudge world numbers here freely. All 'sign' props are wordless emissive panels — no text in the room, ever.",
